  "worked_solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 3 & \\frac{1}{5} & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 3 & \\frac{1}{5} & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{4}{5} & -24\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{5}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 30\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+\\frac{1}{3}y=11 \\\\  & y=30,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=30$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+\\frac{1}{3}(30)=11\\,\u21d2\\,x=11-10=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=1$ and $y=30.$",
